#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059412 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059692 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dffa4760-00cb-5395-8fab-dc7f9fe20597" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse of a Statement"}] :question/id #uuid "144f352c-5696-5ad3-841f-3a6a1cf2e5f2" :question/math-academy-id "e-12710" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the following statement: \n\n$\\qquad$ **If** it is summer, **then** it is not snowy outside." :question/worked-solution "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A{:}$ It is summer.\n\n- The consequent is $B{:}$ It is not snowy outside.\n\nThe inverse of a conditional statement $A \\Rightarrow B$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\neg A \\Rightarrow \\neg B.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B{:}$\n\n- $\\neg A{:}$ It is not summer.\n\n- $\\neg B{:}$ It is snowy outside.\n\nTherefore, the inverse is the following: \n\n$\\qquad$ If it is not summer, then it is snowy outside."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059413 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059691 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec5acb94-b33a-5921-b761-6f78db3f25f7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Converse of a Statement"}] :question/id #uuid "9f3fe8eb-f539-539e-96c6-33b6a238fc82" :question/math-academy-id "e-12711" :question/problem "Find the converse of the following statement:\n\n$\\qquad$ **If** it is summer, **then** it is not snowy outside." :question/worked-solution "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A{:}$ It is summer.\n\n- The consequent is $B{:}$ It is not snowy outside.\n\nThe converse of a conditional statement $A \\Rightarrow B$ is given by \n\n$$\nB \\Rightarrow A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the converse is the following: \n\n$\\qquad$ If it is not snowy outside, then it is summer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059414 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059693 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f58ec96-53b3-5317-9801-c730728f32c6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Contrapositive of a Statement"}] :question/id #uuid "9e1fa00b-8e51-5689-959d-049df21077bd" :question/math-academy-id "e-12712" :question/problem "Find the contrapositive of the following statement: \n\n$\\qquad$ **If** it is summer, **then** it is not snowy outside." :question/worked-solution "In our conditional statement: \n\n- The antecedent is $A{:}$ It is summer.\n\n- The consequent is $B{:}$ It is not snowy outside.\n\nThe contrapositive of a conditional statement $A \\Rightarrow B$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\neg B \\Rightarrow \\neg A.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B{:}$\n\n- $\\neg A{:}$ It is not summer.\n\n- $\\neg B{:}$ It is snowy outside.\n\nTherefore, the contrapositive is the following: \n\n$\\qquad$ If it is snowy outside, then it is not summer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059415 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059694 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d3501b-96ef-5fbd-9d93-788021156ddb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"}] :question/id #uuid "31e2f48c-65cc-53c3-b34c-70e2c53a9274" :question/math-academy-id "e-12713" :question/problem "$\\qquad$ **If** it is summer, **then** it is not snowy outside.\n\nWhich of the following statements are equivalent to the conditional statement above?\n\n- If it is not summer, then it is snowy outside.\n\n- If it is not snowy outside, then it is summer.\n\n- If it is snowy outside, then it is not summer." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.\n\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other, but not to the original statement.\n\n![](images/d9/d946d2a81d46cbde934ebbab54f9b69b514092e02da4f8a3b79768f218929449.png)\n\nSo, we are looking for the contrapositive of the given statement.\n\n- Statement I is the inverse, not the contrapositive. $\\quad \\color{red}\\times$\n\n- Statement II is the converse, not the contrapositive. $\\quad \\color{red}\\times$\n\n- Statement III is the contrapositive. $\\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399524 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059692 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dffa4760-00cb-5395-8fab-dc7f9fe20597" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse of a Statement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a03c021-ed0f-56d1-9f86-6e79e9f2243f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If it is not raining, then it is winter." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399526} {:answer/id #uuid "a3563445-92f5-50b0-ac76-9bc11efc53d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If it is not winter, then it is raining." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399527} {:answer/id #uuid "56c3fd5e-3d94-5fa6-86e5-8f3bba739552" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If it is winter, then it is not raining." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399528} {:answer/id #uuid "1d41538a-0fa0-518c-be9a-da1a8f9015d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If it is not raining, then it is not winter." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399529} {:answer/id #uuid "778cf961-301a-523b-93e0-fd59d3bcd024" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If it is raining, then it is winter." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399530}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a03c021-ed0f-56d1-9f86-6e79e9f2243f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If it is not raining, then it is winter." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399526} :answer-field/id #uuid "f115b663-1b63-53de-8458-d4ee1cff91f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399525}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ec898c4f-16e5-5b8b-9206-977a4ec7986a" :question/math-academy-id "q-106678" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** it is raining, **then** it is not winter." :question/worked-solution "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ It is raining.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ It is not winter.\n\nThe inverse of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\n¬A⇒¬B.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $¬A:$ It is not raining.\n\n- $¬B:$ It is winter.\n\nTherefore, the inverse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If it is not raining, then it is winter."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573918 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059692 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dffa4760-00cb-5395-8fab-dc7f9fe20597" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse of a Statement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05675fad-4306-5dbe-b3d0-a7a881c811d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If Robert doesn't go for a walk, then it rains." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573428} {:answer/id #uuid "464aaedc-1181-5732-bd94-10d2ccc12fa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If Robert goes for a walk, then it doesn't rain." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573509} {:answer/id #uuid "69e950a1-c273-5504-aea7-bba23b852cf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If it doesn't rain, then Robert goes for a walk." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573553} {:answer/id #uuid "9aab5566-6093-5a42-b8cf-866244373f77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If it rains, then Robert doesn't go for a walk." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573625} {:answer/id #uuid "c17eae93-5d60-5ef0-84d0-4393920ca67c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If it doesn't rain, then Robert doesn't go for a walk." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573674}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9aab5566-6093-5a42-b8cf-866244373f77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If it rains, then Robert doesn't go for a walk." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573625} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb272fdc-0f82-5948-ba90-fb672bed1ac0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573863}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bc18945c-2d46-5692-9a78-27019da5591c" :question/math-academy-id "q-106680" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** it doesn't rain, **then** Robert goes for a walk." :question/worked-solution "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ It doesn't rain.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ Robert goes for a walk.\n\nThe inverse of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\n¬A⇒¬B.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $¬A:$ It rains.\n\n- $¬B:$ Robert doesn't go for a walk.\n\nTherefore, the inverse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If it rains, then Robert doesn't go for a walk."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378320 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059693 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f58ec96-53b3-5317-9801-c730728f32c6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Contrapositive of a Statement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91833904-266b-5225-a0db-02f970dbc0a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If it gets warmer, then the sun comes out." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378322} {:answer/id #uuid "215eddd9-79f7-5359-b1cd-97569af0e2b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If the sun does not come out, then it gets warmer." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378323} {:answer/id #uuid "df5b5f4e-faac-5af1-a95d-c12e7d26b374" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If the sun does not come out, then it does not get warmer." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378324} {:answer/id #uuid "7397d158-4b17-51c3-bae5-1e3acf204602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If the sun comes out, then it gets warmer." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378325} {:answer/id #uuid "90d384b6-c07f-56e0-86ea-8f1bb7789e51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If the sun comes out, then it does not get warmer." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7397d158-4b17-51c3-bae5-1e3acf204602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If the sun comes out, then it gets warmer." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378325} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9f8ccbc-1687-5b4d-9590-26ca0dfa92bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6140dc58-ccf3-5a53-9ee2-21989ff9d18e" :question/math-academy-id "q-106796" :question/problem "Find the contrapositive of the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ **If** it does not get warmer, **then** the sun does not come out." :question/worked-solution "In our conditional statement: \n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ It does not get warmer.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ The sun does not come out.\n\nThe contrapositive of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\n¬B⇒¬A.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $¬A:$ It gets warmer.\n\n- $¬B:$ The sun comes out.\n\nTherefore, the contrapositive is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If the sun comes out, then it gets warm."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060112 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059693 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f58ec96-53b3-5317-9801-c730728f32c6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Contrapositive of a Statement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85e53b69-a50d-5705-8a63-ab481f5933d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If $6$ is prime, then ${1, 2}∩{2, 3} = ∅$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057031} {:answer/id #uuid "e3ad9cce-3b74-567d-b629-f0545bdb375f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If ${1, 2}∩{2, 3} \\ne ∅$, then $6$ is not prime." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057032} {:answer/id #uuid "f916a99d-9069-5af0-b072-c8f81de5875a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057033} {:answer/id #uuid "21267543-eb95-5b72-9ac8-f38244e38fa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If $6$ is not prime, then ${1, 2}∩{2, 3} \\ne ∅$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057034} {:answer/id #uuid "28ae9ea9-3fb4-5ed0-abf8-c5af77485437" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If ${1, 2}∩{2, 3} = ∅$, then $6$ is prime." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057035}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4d69dabd-cff4-5d4e-88f8-585fef7183ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057030}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "38ac2a48-89e3-5cdd-bcff-f22b6ccd3098" :question/math-academy-id "q-171332" :question/problem "Find the contrapositive of the following statement:\n\n**If** ${1, 2}∩{2, 3} = ∅$, **then** $6$ is prime."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060113 :kno