 "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477183} {:answer/id #uuid "03a88033-d0c2-5192-ac1b-264d0b7c2da6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477184}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9af1a8b8-d9e6-5807-9fc8-c761158a383a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477183} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8c3534b-c88f-5cd8-a830-dd021584e964" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477561}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "37ad276a-88ce-596c-9a24-406a32aa6e25" :question/math-academy-id "q-171334" :question/problem "$\\,$ **If** $10\\ge 1,$ **then** $3\\in R.$ \n\nWhich of the following statements are equivalent to the conditional statement above?\n- **I.** If $10<1,$ then $3\\notin R.$\n- **II.** If $3\\notin R,$ then $10<1.$\n- **III.** If $3\\in R,$ then $10\\ge 1.$\n\nCompare the logical forms for arbitrary truth values of the antecedent and consequent.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.\n\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other, but not to the original statement.\n\n![](images/d9/d946d2a81d46cbde934ebbab54f9b69b514092e02da4f8a3b79768f218929449.png)\n\nSo, we are looking for the contrapositive of the given statement.\n\n- Statement I is the inverse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement II is the contrapositive. $\\,✓$\n\n- Statement III is the converse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407669 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059692 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dffa4760-00cb-5395-8fab-dc7f9fe20597" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse of a Statement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "510c98ba-ef87-5fff-b4b1-e86de7cdfb0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If it is summer, then you go to the beach." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407645} {:answer/id #uuid "9e2b2fc1-d648-5d31-a1bf-eb01219a5fe4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If you don't go to the beach, then it is not summer" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407651} {:answer/id #uuid "aa3283a3-cded-5b86-bf40-e38e5cd197ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If it is not summer, then you go to the beach." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407654} {:answer/id #uuid "c584f385-4eba-5ef1-a423-eac23cbae655" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If you go to the beach, then it is summer" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407657} {:answer/id #uuid "fb8ad54f-4913-5b36-8cdb-740da26e279e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If it is summer, then you don't go to the beach." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407660}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "510c98ba-ef87-5fff-b4b1-e86de7cdfb0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If it is summer, then you go to the beach." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407645} :answer-field/id #uuid "286c752f-2970-5ff4-abd2-b57ef3623964" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407662}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a480d9fc-6f80-5af5-b6f1-0b67fa2323fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-183281" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** it is not summer, **then** you don't go to the beach." :question/worked-solution "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ It is not summer.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ You don't go to the beach.\n\nThe inverse of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\n¬A⇒¬B.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $¬A:$ It is summer.\n\n- $¬B:$ You go to the beach.\n\nTherefore, the inverse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If it is summer, then you go to the beach."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379281 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059692 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dffa4760-00cb-5395-8fab-dc7f9fe20597" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse of a Statement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "232c804b-383b-5dae-9c59-1c674cf939d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If you don't go to the hospital, then you are not sick." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379283} {:answer/id #uuid "ca1fb6bf-39d9-5e52-9dbe-bf750a7a3c68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If you are sick, then you don't go to the hospital." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379284} {:answer/id #uuid "d3d3a898-a1be-5ad2-9622-8cb4a2a0f15c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If you are not sick, then you go to the hospital." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379285} {:answer/id #uuid "337dfe0d-88f5-5501-bfcc-6cf790b2a9cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If you are sick, then you go to the hospital." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379286} {:answer/id #uuid "42bba623-0d23-5c6a-8895-ab30b259bf58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If you go to the hospital, then you are not sick." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "337dfe0d-88f5-5501-bfcc-6cf790b2a9cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If you are sick, then you go to the hospital." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379286} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca8f03c6-02b3-54f9-9c07-16ff600067c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379282}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "be66b1f8-682e-59f1-a668-bd79f735e6c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-183282" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** you are not sick, **then** you don't go to the hospital." :question/worked-solution "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ You are not sick.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ You don't go to the hospital.\n\nThe inverse of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\n¬A⇒¬B.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $¬A:$ You are sick.\n\n- $¬B:$ You go to the hospital.\n\nTherefore, the inverse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If you are sick, then you go to the hospital."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573872 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059691 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec5acb94-b33a-5921-b761-6f78db3f25f7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Converse of a Statement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "230d8866-8d8f-52b0-8e59-d1dbfb086463" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If $5$ is not odd, then $4$ is not even." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573468} {:answer/id #uuid "36585ca7-2a0b-573f-9b14-c8fbf97df961" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If $5$ is odd, then $4$ is not even." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573493} {:answer/id #uuid "379a04f9-80c1-526c-ab31-eaa334ae3a2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :an