ning.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ You can go to the beach.\n\nThe converse of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\nB⇒A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the converse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If you can go to the beach, then it is not raining."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573899 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059693 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f58ec96-53b3-5317-9801-c730728f32c6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Contrapositive of a Statement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1792e8e1-9b75-5b79-8f9d-fab35e0abd08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If you get your salary, then you do not go to work." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573445} {:answer/id #uuid "df497600-11d4-5267-86ae-0049744e1ab4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If you do not get your salary, then you go to work." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573716} {:answer/id #uuid "eda33fe8-64c8-51a6-90ad-9d35d5ba3a57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If you go to work, then you get your salary." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573739} {:answer/id #uuid "f191a352-7a91-5c11-878a-b4bdcfa6ace1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If you do not get your salary, then you do not go to work." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573748} {:answer/id #uuid "f223db35-b3a4-5114-991c-a65029e576c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If you get your salary, then you go to work." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573749}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f223db35-b3a4-5114-991c-a65029e576c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "If you get your salary, then you go to work." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573749} :answer-field/id #uuid "52a8a1fe-c61a-5cde-b53f-e1d2a410da2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573804}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7e17e456-5cfd-52c7-99bf-b5bb8d3b9d9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-82636" :question/problem "Find the contrapositive of the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ **If** you do not go to work, **then** you do not get your salary." :question/worked-solution "In our conditional statement: \n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ You do not go to work.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ You do not get your salary.\n\nThe contrapositive of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\n¬B⇒¬A.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $¬A:$ You go to work.\n\n- $¬B:$ You get your salary.\n\nTherefore, the contrapositive is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If you get your salary, then you go to work."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380214 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059694 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d3501b-96ef-5fbd-9d93-788021156ddb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a995511-c3ab-56a2-a302-1bedfa2904eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471747} {:answer/id #uuid "6107507d-d229-5b6d-bb78-6dd1692778b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471748}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6107507d-d229-5b6d-bb78-6dd1692778b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471748} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd7e4d8b-e538-50ff-8391-7016b9eb8aa4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472379} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a56ffb3-32e1-5ba6-b9d2-390da306e6c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471749} {:answer/id #uuid "daaaceb5-1235-586b-9abe-50131f6df41e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471750}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a56ffb3-32e1-5ba6-b9d2-390da306e6c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471749} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b29eaa7-fd58-579d-814b-190372ed2a71" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472380} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dbda4a9-a5b8-5487-bcc5-bf76150369a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471751} {:answer/id #uuid "cfc52945-efa3-5eae-946e-3e2073cc7990" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471752}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1dbda4a9-a5b8-5487-bcc5-bf76150369a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471751} :answer-field/id #uuid "462f3da3-0d78-500c-8d71-92f10c5cbc0a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7b3cb87d-282a-5d16-9402-d3db5936c8ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-82660" :question/problem "$\\,$ **If** I am not sleeping, **then** I am awake.\n\nWhich of the following statements are equivalent to the conditional statement above?\n- **I.** If I am not awake, then I am sleeping.\n- **II.** If I am sleeping, then I am not awake.\n- **III.** If I am awake, then I am not sleeping.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.\n\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other, but not to the original statement.\n\n![](images/0d/0deb19675402bf931111bb80cb616682aac08491b5cd3e1ab5812da05b6df8a8.png)\n\nSo, we are looking for the contrapositive.\n\n- Statement I is the contrapositive. $\\,✓$\n\n- Statement II is the inverse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement III is the converse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380221 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059694 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d3501b-96ef-5fbd-9d93-788021156ddb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dda9d468-becb-54e6-9d7c-a36da59bbb0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471753} {:answer/id #uuid "3bc1de6b-6351-548e-b152-50fd8ef8413e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471754}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bc1de6b-6351-548e-b152-50fd8ef8413e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471754} :answer-field/id #uuid "a959e3ca-4163-50bd-9b6f-1b49bb7a3efb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472382} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "714898a2-3141-5053-ab51-02f399c94eb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471755} {:answer/id #uuid "a436efc5-6bb5-5944-b3f8-595b5e63604d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "714898a2-3141-5053-ab51-02f399c94eb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471755} :answer-field/id #uuid "18c69588-c464-5cab-89e1-7667dce161c6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472383} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39d3c8d9-8286-5656-ad84-dec522575e91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471757} {:answer/id #uuid "c0099cb5-5210-539d-8a9c-36530f395a74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471758}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39d3c8d9-8286-5656-ad84-dec522575e91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471757} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a7a2082-751e-5b23-942c-7a7417ba6a57" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472384}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4b3c08af-1740-5428-a4c7-1f507e3193d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-82664" :question/problem "$\\,$ **If** we do not go to the cinema, **then** we watch a movie at home.\n\nWhich of the following statements are equivalent to the conditional statement above?\n- **I.** If we do not watch a movie at home, then we go to the cinema.\n- **II.** If we watch a movie at home, then we do not go to the cinema.\n- **III.** If we go to the cinema, then we do not watch a movie at home.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.\n\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other, but not to the original statement.\n\n![](images/0d/0deb19675402bf931111bb80cb616682aac08491b5cd3e1ab5812da05b6df8a8.png)\n\nSo, we are looking for the contrapositive.\n\n- Statement I is the contrapositive. $\\,✓$\n\n- Statement I is the converse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement III is the inverse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}]}
